  "title": "Michigan Reports First Deaths in Major Cyclosporiasis Outbreak Linked to Contaminated Lettuce",
  "summary": "Two Fatalities Confirmed as Foodborne Illness Spreads Across Multiple US States Michigan health officials have confirmed the first reported deaths connected to the ongoing US outbreak of cyclosporiasis, a foodborne illness caused by the parasite Cyclospora. The outbreak, which has affected thousands of people across the country, has been linked to contaminated lettuce and has raised concerns about food safety, produce handling, and the challenges of tracking certain parasites. According to Mic",
